  "idea": "Raycast vs Alfred: which Mac productivity launcher takes the crown",
  "text": "Raycast versus Alfred remains the ultimate showdown for controlling your Mac desktop workflow. Alfred loyalists prize its tiny memory footprint, but manual workflow setup creates recurring maintenance overhead. Lacking modern team extensions and integrated AI prompts forces you to juggle several disconnected utility apps. Raycast replaces standalone apps by packing floating notes, window controls, and community extensions into one launcher. Your entire workstation feels unified and lightning fast.",
